# SXUPTP coloring rules -- makes the ~69s wedge and SXUPTP traffic pop.
# Requires the sxuptp.lua dissector to be loaded (for the sxuptp.* fields).
#
# Install: View > Coloring Rules > Import... and pick this file (or append its
# lines to your personal "colorfilters" file). First match wins; order matters.
# RGB values are 16-bit (8-bit value x 257).
#
# @name@display-filter@[bg r,g,b][fg r,g,b]
@SXUPTP wedge RST@tcp.flags.reset==1 && (tcp.srcport==19540 || tcp.dstport==19540)@[65535,13107,13107][65535,65535,65535]
@SXUPTP resend (Salc)@sxuptp.salc.resend==1@[65535,42662,0][0,0,0]
@SXUPTP transfer FAIL@sxuptp.status==0xffff || sxuptp.scsi.status>0@[65535,45232,48573][0,0,0]
@SXUPTP identify@sxuptp.id.model || sxuptp.jcp.cmd==0x0004@[51143,59367,65535][0,0,0]
@SXUPTP SCSI CBW/CSW@sxuptp.scsi.op || sxuptp.scsi.status@[52428,65535,52428][0,0,0]
@SXUPTP control SETUP@sxuptp.setup.bRequest@[65535,65535,52428][0,0,0]
@SXUPTP (other)@sxuptp@[61680,61680,61680][0,0,0]
